--TEST--
A class that writes `Core\Db\Codec`'s `fromRow` and carries no `#[Db\Derive]` is hydrated through the member it wrote, handed the `Core\Db\Row` a `query` would have answered with — `rule:core-classes/derive-generates-what-is-missing`, `rule:core-classes/derive-attribute`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The row format is one-directional, so `Core\Db\Codec` declares `fromRow`
// alone and a class that writes it has nothing left for an attribute to
// generate — writing both is `E0757`. Declaring the member is therefore the
// opt-in, as squarely as `#[Db\Derive]` is: `nvs_types::derive`'s
// `check_row_sites` admits the call site for a class that records no column
// mapping but declares this member, and `nvs_stdlib::db::row`'s `hydrate`
// dispatches to it.
//
// What the member builds here is something no mapping could: the properties
// are named after neither column, and one of them is arithmetic over the row.
// So a `queryAs<T>` that quietly fell back to a generated decoder — or that
// handed the member anything other than the real row — fails this case rather
// than printing plausibly.
// covers: Core\Db\Connection::queryAs
class Account {
    public uint $twice;

    public string $who;

    public function constructor(uint $twice, string $who)
    {
        $this->twice = $twice;
        $this->who = $who;
    }

    // `rule:core-classes/db-column-types`: every reader answers `?T`, a NULL
    // column being an ordinary absence, so the narrowing is this member's own
    // business and not the caller's.
    public static function fromRow(Core\Db\Row $row): static
    {
        ?uint $id = $row->uint("id");
        ?string $name = $row->string("name");
        if ($id != null) {
            if ($name != null) {
                return new static($id + $id, $name);
            }
        }
        throw new RuntimeError("a row of `accounts` held a NULL where the schema forbids one");
    }
}

var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");
$db->execute("create table accounts (id integer primary key, name text not null)", []);
$db->executeMany("insert into accounts (name) values (?)", [["ada"], ["grace"]]);

foreach ($db->queryAs<Account>("select id, name from accounts order by id", [])->all() as Account $each) {
    echo "account ", $each->who, " ", $each->twice, "\n";
}

// `rule:classes/no-traits` declares the member once, on `Core\Db\Queryable`, so
// the door a transaction's call reaches is the connection's.
$db->transaction(fn (Core\Db\Transaction $tx): void => {
    foreach ($tx->queryAs<Account>("select id, name from accounts order by id desc", [])->all() as Account $mirrored) {
        echo "in transaction ", $mirrored->who, " ", $mirrored->twice, "\n";
    }
});
--FILE nvs.toml--
# § 3: a SQLite connection's file path comes from its config block, so
# `db.connect` covers it.
[capabilities.db]
connect = ["main"]

[db.main]
driver = "sqlite"
path = ":memory:"
--EXPECT--
account ada 2
account grace 4
in transaction grace 4
in transaction ada 2
